From: PS4 port
Subject: [PATCH] orbis: a link-level address header, and a TLS initialiser create-fself insists on

Two things this SDK does not have, both of which stop the module at a different stage.

⚠ <net/if_dl.h>, WHICH IS THE ONLY BSD HEADER MISSING FROM AN OTHERWISE COMPLETE SET.

    _deps/melonds-src/src/net/Net_PCap.cpp:35:22: fatal error: 'net/if_dl.h' file not found

melonDS walks getifaddrs() and reads each adapter's MAC out of the AF_LINK entry, which on every
BSD means struct sockaddr_dl from <net/if_dl.h>. This SDK ships <ifaddrs.h>, <net/if.h> and
AF_LINK in <sys/socket.h>; it just has no <net/if_dl.h>. src/libretro/orbis-compat/net/if_dl.h is
the FreeBSD declaration, unchanged, and the include directory is added next to the one melonDS's
own src/net already gets.

Net_PCap.cpp is fetched, so it cannot be patched from here - and it does not need to be. It
dlopen()s libpcap at run time and reports the direct-mode adapter list as empty when that fails,
which is the truthful answer on a console. What the file has to do is COMPILE, because the core's
own net/net.cpp and platform/lan.cpp name melonDS::LibPCap and melonDS::AdapterData
unconditionally; without it the link was missing six symbols and a typeinfo.

⚠ AND ONE UNDEFINED WEAK SYMBOL, WHICH ld.lld ACCEPTS AND create-fself DOES NOT.

    Failed to build FSELF: missing library for symbol (_ZTHN7melonDS3NDS7CurrentE)

melonDS::NDS::Current is a constant-initialised `thread_local NDS*`. core/core.cpp reads it
through the header, so it goes through the TLS wrapper _ZTW..., and that wrapper calls the
initialiser _ZTH... behind a WEAK reference - which is never defined, because a constant
initialiser needs no initialiser function. Correct ELF, and every desktop build does exactly
this. create-fself maps every remaining undefined symbol to a library NID, finds nothing that
exports this one, and refuses the whole module (with exit status 0, which is why the harness
checks for the file rather than the status).

ps4/orbis_weak_stubs.c in the RetroArch tree answers the same complaint for zstd's trace hooks
and for glsm_ctl and explains it in full, but it cannot answer this one: the name is the C++
mangling of one core's variable and would mean nothing in a file every core links. So the
definition goes here - a no-op, which is exactly what the wrapper does when the weak reference
resolves to null, and weak itself so that a melonDS which one day does need dynamic
initialisation here overrides it.

diff --git a/src/libretro/CMakeLists.txt b/src/libretro/CMakeLists.txt
index 0ed8016..8d91de5 100644
--- a/src/libretro/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/libretro/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -191,6 +191,7 @@ if (HAVE_NETWORKING)
     )
 
     target_include_directories(melondsds_libretro SYSTEM PRIVATE "${melonDS_SOURCE_DIR}/src/net")
+    target_include_directories(melondsds_libretro SYSTEM PRIVATE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/orbis-compat")
 
     if (HAVE_NETWORKING_DIRECT_MODE)
         target_sources(melondsds_libretro PRIVATE
@@ -200,6 +201,8 @@ if (HAVE_NETWORKING)
     endif()
 endif ()
 
+target_sources(melondsds_libretro PRIVATE orbis-compat/tls_init.cpp)
+
 if (TRACY_ENABLE)
     target_sources(melondsds_libretro PRIVATE tracy/memory.cpp)
 
diff --git a/src/libretro/orbis-compat/net/if_dl.h b/src/libretro/orbis-compat/net/if_dl.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..68d120e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/libretro/orbis-compat/net/if_dl.h
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+/* net/if_dl.h - the BSD link-level socket address, for the PlayStation 4 SDK.
+ *
+ * melonDS's src/net/Net_PCap.cpp walks getifaddrs() and reads an adapter's MAC out of the
+ * AF_LINK entry, which on every BSD means <net/if_dl.h> and struct sockaddr_dl. This SDK ships
+ * <ifaddrs.h>, <net/if.h> and AF_LINK in <sys/socket.h> - it simply has no <net/if_dl.h>, so
+ * the one thing missing is this declaration. It is the FreeBSD layout, unchanged.
+ */
+#ifndef _NET_IF_DL_H_
+#define _NET_IF_DL_H_
+
+#include <sys/types.h>
+#include <sys/socket.h>
+
+struct sockaddr_dl {
+	unsigned char	sdl_len;	/* Total length of sockaddr */
+	unsigned char	sdl_family;	/* AF_LINK */
+	unsigned short	sdl_index;	/* if != 0, system given index for interface */
+	unsigned char	sdl_type;	/* interface type */
+	unsigned char	sdl_nlen;	/* interface name length, no trailing 0 reqd. */
+	unsigned char	sdl_alen;	/* link level address length */
+	unsigned char	sdl_slen;	/* link layer selector length */
+	char		sdl_data[46];	/* minimum work area, can be larger;
+					   contains both if name and ll address */
+};
+
+#define LLADDR(s) ((caddr_t)((s)->sdl_data + (s)->sdl_nlen))
+
+#endif /* _NET_IF_DL_H_ */
diff --git a/src/libretro/orbis-compat/tls_init.cpp b/src/libretro/orbis-compat/tls_init.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f0b956f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/libretro/orbis-compat/tls_init.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+/* A definition for melonDS::NDS::Current's TLS initialiser, for the PlayStation 4.
+ *
+ * melonDS::NDS::Current is `static thread_local NDS* Current;`, defined in NDS.cpp as nullptr.
+ * A translation unit that reads it through the header - core/core.cpp here - goes through the
+ * TLS wrapper _ZTW..., and that wrapper calls the initialiser _ZTH... behind a WEAK reference,
+ * because a constant-initialised thread_local needs no initialiser and none is emitted. Leaving
+ * it undefined is correct ELF and every desktop build does exactly that.
+ *
+ * create-fself does not agree. It maps every remaining undefined symbol to a library NID,
+ * finds no library exporting this one, and refuses the module - with exit status 0:
+ *
+ *     Failed to build FSELF: missing library for symbol (_ZTHN7melonDS3NDS7CurrentE)
+ *
+ * ps4/orbis_weak_stubs.c in the RetroArch tree answers the same complaint for zstd's trace hooks
+ * and for glsm_ctl, and says why in full. It cannot answer this one: the name is a C++ mangling
+ * of one core's variable and would mean nothing in a file every core links.
+ *
+ * So: a no-op, which is precisely what the wrapper does when the reference resolves to null,
+ * and WEAK so that a melonDS which one day does need dynamic initialisation here wins over it.
+ */
+extern "C" void melondsds_orbis_nds_current_tls_init(void) asm("_ZTHN7melonDS3NDS7CurrentE");
+
+__attribute__((weak)) void melondsds_orbis_nds_current_tls_init(void) {}
